Detect what a file is: its chain of codecs and archive format (`zstd → tar`), whether it is
a self-extracting archive, and what it is when it isn't an archive at all.

Usage: beezip detect [OPTIONS] <PATH>

Arguments:
  <PATH>
          The file to look at

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Global options:
      --output <FORMAT>
          How to print results; ndjson streams every job event

          Possible values:
          - human:  Text for people
          - json:   One JSON document on stdout: the output, or `{"error": {...}}`
          - ndjson: Every job event as a JSON line on stdout, ending with `Finished`, `Failed` or
            `Cancelled`
          
          [default: human]

  -q, --quiet
          No progress bars or info messages; warnings still print
